invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_sign64.c
catches: test/widemul-builds.sh
reason: the signer checks each candidate signature on the AVX-512 IFMA
  kernel through a declaration of its own, under every session's value:
  a session whose caller named no AVX-512 IFMA runs its instructions and
  dies of SIGILL on a CPU without them, and the kernel's frames are left
  unwiped. The signer reaches the kernel through rsa_vp1_cpu alone, where
  the value names it, and wipes after it. The script requires that no
  root source but rsa_mont.c calls rsa_ifma_public, whatever it includes.

--- old
    rsa_mont64_public(power, candidate, k->n_len, &mod);
--- new
    void rsa_ifma_public(uint8_t *out, const uint8_t *base, size_t len,
                         const rsa_mont64_modulus *mod, const uint64_t *digit_r2);
    rsa_ifma_public(power, candidate, k->n_len, &mod, mod.r2);
